include "../../../linux.mereo"

-- A fallible system call with nowhere for its failure to go.
--
-- Every syscall that can fail declares its own contract -- `read` says
-- `ensure count as signed >= 0`, and the reading is part of the declaration, so
-- binding the result to an unsigned field cannot turn the test into one that is
-- always true. But a contract needs somewhere to fail TO: the release tower is
-- built from the resources a scope holds, and a call written bare at program
-- level has no floor beneath it.
--
-- So the call must live in a resource, which is where its `ensure` and its
-- cleanup both come from. That is the compile-time half of "a failure cannot be
-- ignored"; the run-time half is `tests/progs/unsigned_contract`, which reads a
-- directory and exits 1 because the contract held.

program goes
  block is 8 bytes
  n is 0

  linux.read (descriptor is 0, buffer is block, capacity is 8, count is n)   -- MISTAKE

  ensure n >= 0
end
